{"author":{"id":"417295a7cc0952a9a38b67be3a894daed91f9069f7407e038d12a4f9b9a8451e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792346899,"nonce":"80/PWkOjF/CAhnjNTA3CsOZRUSk=","title":"Pool the fibers that calls from natives use","message":"Every Vm::call of a closure allocates a Fiber object on the heap and drops it as garbage; an effect run is one such call. 10,000 class effects in one flush cost 39 ms, about 3.9 us each, and leave 10,000 dead fibers for the next collection (which cannot run inside a nested call). Reuse a few fibers, with their stacks, for these calls.","files":null}]}